Control Structures
******************

.[perex]
The `controlFlow` section decides on control structures: `elseif` as one word, an `else` after a branch that always exits, an `if` that returns `true` and `false`, an early return instead of an `if` at the end of a function, the comment on a `case` that falls through, and the empty statement `;;`.

Three decisions make the code flatter. `elseAfterReturn` and `elseifAfterReturn` remove an `else` and an `elseif` when every branch before them exits through `return`, `throw`, `break` or `continue`. `trailingIf` turns an `if` that wraps the end of a function or a loop into an early return, when its body has at least as many statements as the parameter `trailingIfMinStatements` says. The lines that move one level to the left are re-indented by the [indentation |indentation] section, so the example sets it too:

```neon
controlFlow:
	elseif: 'elseif'
	elseAfterReturn: forbidden
	elseifAfterReturn: forbidden
	ifReturningTrueFalse: forbidden
indentation:
	unit: tab
```

```php .[before]
function discount(int $count): float
{
	if ($count > 10) {
		return 0.1;
	} else if ($count > 5) {  // Useless else, because the branches before it always leave.
		return 0.05;
	} else {  // Useless else, because the branches before it always leave.
		return 0.0;  // Expected the statement indented by 1 tab, 2 tabs found.
	}
}

function isBig(int $count): bool
{
	if ($count > 100) {  // Useless `if`, because its condition itself is the result.
		return true;
	}
	return false;
}
```

```php .[after]
function discount(int $count): float
{
	if ($count > 10) {
		return 0.1;
	}
	if ($count > 5) {
		return 0.05;
	}
	return 0.0;
}

function isBig(int $count): bool
{
	return $count > 100;
}
```


controlFlow.trailingIf
======================

An `if` ending a function or a loop body becomes a guard that leaves early, and an `else` that leaves becomes the first branch.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.ControlStructures.EarlyExit` .[decision-facts]


controlFlow.trailingIfMinStatements
===================================

The statements the body of a trailing `if` has at least for it to become a guard.

- a number from 1

Default `2` · standards: perCs `2`, psr12 `2`, nette `2`, symfony `2`, laravel `2` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.ControlStructures.EarlyExit` .[decision-facts]


controlFlow.elseif
==================

The keyword of a branch that follows `if`.

- `'elseif'`: `elseif` in one word, never `else if`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `elseif`, psr12 `elseif`, nette `elseif`, symfony `elseif`, laravel `elseif` · covers `elseif`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.ElseIfDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


controlFlow.switch.fallThroughComment
=====================================

The text of the comment a non-empty `case` falling through to the next one carries, without the marker of the comment, matched case-insensitively and reported only where none is found; a case that cannot fall through loses it.

- text
- a list of these words, where each one passes and code matching none of them is written like the first
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `no break`, psr12 `no break`, nette `break omitted`, symfony `no break`, laravel `keep` · covers `no_break_comment`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.SwitchDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


controlFlow.emptyStatement
==========================

The second `;` of `foo();;`.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · covers `no_empty_statement`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.PHP.UselessSemicolon` .[decision-facts]


controlFlow.ifReturningTrueFalse
================================

`if ($a > 1) { return true; } return false;` is `return $a > 1;`.

Not about branches returning other values, which `controlFlow.ifElseReturning` writes as a ternary.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `simplified_if_return`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.ControlStructures.UselessIfConditionWithReturn` .[decision-facts]


controlFlow.ifElseReturning
===========================

`if ($c) { return 1; } else { return 2; }` is `return $c ? 1 : 2;`.

Not about the ternary of `true` and `false` it may write, which `expressions.ternary.ofTrueFalse` writes as the condition.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.ControlStructures.RequireTernaryOperator` .[decision-facts]


controlFlow.elseAfterReturn
===========================

An `else` after branches that always leave, by `return`, `throw`, `break`, `continue`, `exit` or `goto`, whose statements then follow the `if`, and an empty `else`.

Not about an `if` and an `else` each returning a value, which `controlFlow.ifElseReturning` writes as one `return` first.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `keep` · covers `no_useless_else`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.ControlStructures.EarlyExit` .[decision-facts]


controlFlow.elseifAfterReturn
=============================

An `elseif` after an `if` that always leaves, which becomes an `if` of its own with the later branches.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `no_superfluous_elseif`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.ControlStructures.EarlyExit` .[decision-facts]
